# Uniform by-reference capture (F3 — the mutation form, parity guard for the closure airlock arm).
# A closure `f` captures a by-reference local `xs` (a cell holding a list) and MUTATES its inner heap
# value through a method call (`xs.push(2)`) — the cell is not rebound, but its contents change. When
# `f` crosses a `spawn` task boundary via the call form `spawn f()`, the task must receive an ISOLATED
# deep copy of the cell (and its list) — otherwise the task would push into the
# parent's shared list. Output is `[1]` (the parent's `xs` is untouched by the task's push).
# DO NOT "fix" toward sharing — the isolation IS the memory-safety line (design §4
# F1/F3): a plain capture into a task is snapshot-copied; use `Shared[T]` to share across tasks.
fn main():
    xs := [1]
    f := fn(): xs.push(2)
    parallel:
        spawn f()
    print(xs)                   # [1] (task pushed into its own isolated copy)

main()
